      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2015, SLACK Incorporated.",
        "AbstractText": "Subretinal cysticercosis presenting with anterior uveitis and hypopyon is rare. A 7-year-old boy presented with pain and hypopyon in the right eye. Ultrasonography showed a cystic lesion with scolex. Because visual prognosis was poor, he was treated conservatively. Timely diagnosis would facilitate early therapy and prevent visual loss."
      },
